---
title: Pineapple Ghost Chili Hot Sauce
description: A fruity, very hot sauce of pineapple and ghost chilies.
tags: [hot-sauce, spicy, canning]
course: condiment
source:
  name: food.com
  url: http://www.food.com/recipe/pineapple-ghost-chili-sauce-438373
---

> Gloves are a must when preparing the ghost chilies.

Place the @pineapple{16%oz}(454 g, cubed), @ghost chilies{4}, @onion{1}(small, 6 oz, cubed), @carrot{1}(3 oz, rough chopped), @golden raisins{1%oz}(28 g, 1/4 cup), @garlic cloves{4}(1 oz), @lime{1}(zest and meat, white pith discarded), @ginger{1/2%oz}(14 g, rough chopped), @turmeric{1/2%tsp}, @cumin{1/2%tsp}, @cinnamon{1/4%tsp}, @sugar{50%g}(1/4 cup), and @salt{1%tsp} (everything but the vinegar) in a #food processor{} and pulse till pureed.

Add the mixed ingredients to a #pot{} with the @vinegar{1 1/2%cup}(355 ml) and cook ~cook{15%minutes}. If needed blend again for a smooth sauce.

Fill the hot sauce into sterilized hot #bottles{}(or jars).

Place in a hot water bath for ~process{10%minutes}.

Let age for at least 1 week.
